Understood, and I've made that the governing requirement of all three plans. Whether the machine acts must not depend on what any text says; text may only change which thing it picks and how good the result is.

Today the text decides whether a tick runs at all. Each of these stopped a click between 13 and 20:

- a target with no published interpretation is refused;
- a mission document with no `## Relations` section can't be scored;
- an interpretation answer is validated against the pattern library's text and rejected;
- the wording of an author's reply decides the outcome kind;
- an author refuses because of what a source document says, and the tick ends there;
- the wording of a status line decides whether a task is in the field.

What this changes in the draft (commit `b0db52cf7`):

- **Lean (Plan C):** the tick model is parametric in the content type. `step` may read typed tags such as kinds, ids and outcome constructors, and never text. The theorems then hold for every content, "XXXX" included, and a `step` that branches on text doesn't typecheck. I added a theorem T0: with a nonempty field, for any content, every tick ends in an action receipt or a typed, routed failure, and successive ticks don't repeat.
- **Verification (Plan B):** the first check is the XXXX run. It is a hermetic sequence of ticks in which every mission body, interpretation, seat reply and free-text field is the string "XXXX". I've written down the expected result now: it fails today at the first gate in the list above. Passing it is the acceptance for the skeleton.
- **Actions (Plan A):** rows are reordered so the skeleton passes the XXXX run first. Each content gate becomes a typed default or a term in the scoring. Interpretations, relations and criteria extraction come afterwards and can only change choices.

One thing a seat reply still has to carry is a minimal non-text tag, such as "done" or "refused"; a reply of bare "XXXX" would end as a typed unparseable outcome and the next tick would move on. I've asked codex-6 what that minimum is, whether "parametric in content" states your requirement correctly, and for the full list of places where control flow reads text.

This went to codex-6 as a third part of the same negotiation (job `invoke-1790751524948-28755-4b9f0bfe`, `park-e1518249…`, 60-minute deadline).
